          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্রমাণ (prômān) is Sanskrit pramāṇa, a measure or standard and, in logic, a proof (Monier-Williams). To have proof is -এর কাছে প্রমাণ থাকা."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
